Cycles/documentation/Cycles/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumCycleBasis()":{"title":"minimumCycleBasis()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum cycle basis (de Pina 1995): "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c"},{"type":"text","text":" cycles, for c"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, independent over GF(2) and spanning the cycle space, with the fewest edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"total of any such basis. Self-loops and parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own, and two copies of an edge form a cycle of length 2. Each cycle starts at its least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cycles come in nondecreasing length, then by their edge positions. Ties between equally"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"short cycles are broken by the rows’ order."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCycleBasis()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"te